WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.700
Bill Skarsgård isn't a household name yet,
but give it time: he's the younger brother

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:10.260
of The Legend of Tarzan star Alexander Skarsgård
and son of veteran actor Stellan Skarsgård,

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:14.900
and this emerging star is set to make a name
for himself as the terrifying Pennywise in

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.640
the upcoming big-screen adaptation of Stephen
King's classic novel It.

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:23.820
The demonic clown was brilliantly played by
Tim Curry in the 1990 TV miniseries version

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:28.720
of the book, so Skarsgård has some big clown
shoes to fill — but he also has more acting

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.000
experience than you might think.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.680
Here are a few projects you may have seen
him in:

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.060
Arn: The Kingdom at Road's End

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.780
Arn: The Knight Templar and Arn: The Kingdom
at Road's End were combined into one epic

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:44.530
cut for international release in 2010, though
in Sweden they were released as two separate

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:47.420
films based on fictional hero Arn Magnusson.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:53.060
Bill's father Stellan played Arn's uncle Birger
and reprised the role for the sequel, bringing

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:58.040
his son Bill in to play Erik, son of the King,
played by Bill's older brother Gustaf.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:03.059
The Skarsgård-filled epic two-parter is the
most expensive Swedish film of all time, costing

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.040
around thirty million dollars.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:06.360
Kenny Begins

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:12.759
Skarsgård went from a deadly serious historical
epic to a completely ridiculous sci-fi comedy

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:17.880
in 2009's Kenny Begins, a feature length prequel
to Swedish TV series Kenny Starfighter.

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:23.180
Kenny is a hopeless "Galaxy Hero" who crash
lands on Earth and meets Skarsgård's Pontus,

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:28.340
an equally unfortunate 15-year-old with terrible
eyesight and a problem with local bullies.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:29.740
Simple Simon

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:35.860
Skarsgård's next performance not only impressed
domestic critics, it also won plenty of praise

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:36.360
Stateside.

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:41.060
The Hollywood Reporter said 2010's Simple
Simon "performs the neat trick of finding

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:45.759
laughs and wisdom about a central character
who suffers from Asperger's syndrome, yet

00:01:45.759 --> 00:01:50.299
does so without trivializing the serious nature
of the affliction," and called Skarsgård's

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.640
performance "superb."

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:53.420
Behind Blue Skies

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:57.940
While The Hollywood Reporter was impressed
by Simple Simon, their review of the second

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:03.140
Bill Skarsgård film to come out in 2010,
the '70s satire Behind Blue Skies, wasn't

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:03.960
quite as kind.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:08.620
"Satirical pokes at Swedish society at the
time are unlikely to strike too many chords

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:09.220
overseas.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:13.580
While there are some appealing performances,
the picture seems bound for a cloudy time

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:14.940
beyond home territory."

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.300
Still, it wasn't all bad.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:20.940
Singling Skarsgård out to praise his performance
as Martin, a troubled boy with an abusive

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:25.750
father, Variety argued that he "makes the
most of a real star turn" in this "joyously

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:27.600
clever take on the coming-of-age story."

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:28.860
Anna Karenina

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:33.620
Making his English-language debut, Skarsgård
appeared in a minor supporting role in the

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:39.330
2012 British historical romance Anna Karenina,
an adaptation of Leo Tolstoy's classic novel

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:40.360
of the same name.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:44.640
Unfortunately for Skarsgård, the project
he chose as his maiden voyage into English

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:49.490
cinema was a story that for years had been
deemed impossible to successfully adapt due

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:51.820
to the sprawling nature of the source material.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:55.220
Reviews were mixed, and the box office results
were lukewarm.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:56.980
Hemlock Grove

00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:02.840
Netflix original series Hemlock Grove got
off to a great start in 2013, pulling in more

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:05.440
viewers over its release weekend than House
of Cards.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:10.680
Interest in the Eli Roth werewolf thriller
soon began to wane, however, and Netflix announced

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.420
that the third season would be the its last.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:17.860
Skarsgård played sulky vampire-like creature
Roman Godfrey, who uses his supernatural powers

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:18.950
to get what he wants …

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:20.220
"Shut up and kiss me."

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.120
Allegiant

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:32.340
Dystopian teen franchises became big business
in Hollywood after The Hunger Games, but they

00:03:32.341 --> 00:03:33.900
can't all be blockbusters.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:38.350
Case in point: The Divergent series, which
suffered diminishing returns at the box office

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:42.930
and progressively worse reviews over the course
of its first three installments, bottoming

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:44.860
out with 2016's Allegiant.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:50.040
It was all a learning experience for Skarsgård,
who played Matthew, a scientist sympathetic

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.540
to the protagonists' cause.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:56.620
If the franchise failed to live up to expectations,
the second-generation star said he used it

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:59.200
as an example of a lesson he'd taken from
his father.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:03.460
"Even if it was the worst, most horrendous
production and the movie turned out garbage,

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:06.810
whatever it is, the experience was something
that he learned from and he wouldn't want

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:07.560
to live without."

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.100
Atomic Blonde

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:14.420
Before terrorizing the kids of Derry, Maine
in It, Skarsgård appeared in what he described

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:18.840
as a "small but fun part playing a German
punk" in Atomic Blonde, the feature length

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:23.530
adaptation of Antony Johnston's Cold War-set
spy thriller graphic novel The Coldest City

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.280
starring Charlize Theron.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:30.410
Atomic Blonde earned largely positive reviews
from critics, and it's got franchise potential:

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:35.550
a prequel to The Coldest City entitled The
Coldest Winter was published in 2016.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.980
Whether Skarsgård will return remains to
be seen.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:42.280
Either way, expect the brooding Swede to pop
up with increasing regularity in Hollywood

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:43.720
over the next few years.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:45.020
Thanks for watching!

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:47.810
